		(uuid "a2929fce-bb4a-4414-9cb1-4041e1680c7b")
	)
	(text "NOTES\n1. RAK4630-8-SM-I (u.FL/MHF variant): RF pads 15 + 37 are internally disconnected —\n    LoRa antenna via MHF pigtail to bulkhead; no RF routing on this board.\n2. 3V3 rail arrives via harness from charger board; Walter power-kill cycles this rail.\n    RTC rides through power-kills on C4 (supercap backup).\n3. MeshCore RAK4631 target probes Wire (P0.13/P0.14) at boot — AutoDiscoverRTCClock\n    finds RV-3028 at 0x52 and writes reg 0x37=0xB4: trickle charger ON (3 kΩ), direct\n    switching mode. C4 charges automatically — zero firmware config needed.\n4. C4: Seiko CPH3225A 11 mF (XH414HG 70 mF is EOL — broker stock only). C6: optional\n    2nd CPH3225A in parallel (22 mF), DNP by default. Never fit a primary coin cell on\n    VBACKUP: MeshCore enables the trickle charger at every boot.\n5. I2C pull-ups 10 k on this board (same as RAK12002). INA3221 on charger board\n    shares the bus through the harness (addr 0x4x, RTC at 0x52 — no conflict).\n6. SWD + nRESET to Walter via harness; USB-C only powers the nRF52840 USB PHY\n    (VBUS pin), never the system — board still needs 3V3 from the harness.\n7. LED1 (P1.03, green) / LED2 (P1.04, blue) match RAK4631 BSP — MeshCore status."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.26 289.59 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b430356c-60b7-4028-9105-1135cf353a1b")
	)
	(text "All four supply pins tied to +3V3 (normal-voltage mode, 2.0–3.6 V).\nNever feed raw battery here — 3V3 comes from the charger-board LDO."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 151.13 217.17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f6ec0690-8493-4d00-a0e1-9a663c139966")
	)
